description: rt/llvm's drift from rt/wasm is intentional (no wasm-specific intrinsics). Rather than merging either into the other, extract a target-neutral core written against a general arch layer; wasm's intrinsics and llvm's natives are two implementations, each with its own host file. The drift is the inventory. Context: mparrett's PR #25 review asked whether llvm would move onto rt/wasm.
